WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Welcome to our training on the Brand Analytics Search Catalog Performance Report.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:11.221
Brands enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry enjoy access to a suite of additional selling benefits,

00:00:11.221 --> 00:00:14.240
including the Brand Analytics tool in Seller Central.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.901
In this video, we'll review the features and functionality of one of the reports you'll find in

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:21.685
Brand Analytics,

00:00:21.685 --> 00:00:22.860
Search Catalog Performance.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.642
This report provides brands with insights into the ways customers interact with their products

00:00:28.642 --> 00:00:30.500
after searching the Amazon store.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.220
It can help them identify customer drop-off points for their products,

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.940
or find gaps in discoverability and sales conversion.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.769
You can access the Search Catalog Performance Report and others in the Brand Analytics tool

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:48.080
if you're a seller internal to a brand enrolled in Brand Registry.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.490
Simply select Brands in the main menu in Seller Central, then click Brand Analytics,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.960
or click All Brand Benefits, then locate the Brand Analytics card.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.496
For more information about accessing Brand Analytics and other Brand Registry tools,

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:10.540
see our modules in Seller University about requesting or managing access to brand selling benefits.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.278
After accessing the Brand Analytics tool, you can select Search Catalog Performance

00:01:15.278 --> 00:01:19.200
from the list of reports at the top of the screen.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.320
The report lists your brand's products by title.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.120
In the second column, you'll see Product ASINs and Categories.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.380
Then you'll see a sequence of metrics that represents customer activity throughout the shopping

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:31.700
funnel.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.155
Impressions is the number of times a product appeared on Search Results pages

00:01:37.155 --> 00:01:39.640
and includes both organic and sponsored products.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.944
This number doesn't include product appearances in widgets,

00:01:42.944 --> 00:01:46.660
like those for highly rated products or new arrivals.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.980
Next to Impressions, you'll see the median price the product appeared with.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:57.286
For example, a pair of sunglasses that are a part of your brand appeared on Search Results pages

00:01:57.286 --> 00:01:59.840
100 times with a median price of $50.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.160
Clicks is the number of times customers clicked a product after it appeared on Search Results pages.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.814
Next to clicks, you'll see the click rate for the product, which is the percentage of time it was

00:02:11.814 --> 00:02:12.580
clicked by customers.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.199
For example, if your sunglasses were clicked 50 times after having 100 impressions,

00:02:18.199 --> 00:02:20.460
their click rate would be 50%.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:26.812
Cart Adds is the number of times customers searched, clicked, then used the Add to Cart button on

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.224
the product's Detail page

00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:31.400
to put it in their cart for purchase later.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:38.120
For example, after receiving 50 clicks, your sunglasses might have 25 cart adds.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.720
Purchases is the number of times that customers searched, clicked, then ordered the product.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.260
This metric includes your sales as well as the sales of other sellers who list the product.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.505
Next to the number of purchases, you'll see the amount in associated sales as well as the conversion

00:02:54.505 --> 00:02:55.720
rate for the product,

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.860
which is the percentage of time it was purchased after being clicked by customers.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:06.700
For example, maybe 10 pairs of your sunglasses were purchased by customers for a total of $525.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:14.151
The conversion rate in this scenario would be 20%, because 10 pairs were purchased after the product

00:03:14.151 --> 00:03:16.840
received 50 clicks on Search Results pages.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:23.735
Note that the metrics in the Search Catalog Performance Report are specific to Search and may not

00:03:23.735 --> 00:03:27.120
match metrics available in other Amazon reports and dashboards.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:32.720
That's because every report and dashboard defines and presents customer activity differently.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.607
When you first access the Search Catalog Performance Report, it'll be defaulted to show products

00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:41.320
across all your brands for the previous week.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:46.520
You can use the drop-down menus at the top to view a specific time period.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:53.280
When doing so, keep in mind that data is generally available in brand analytics within 72 hours.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.320
After selecting a time period, click the Apply button to refresh the report.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.160
You can also use filters to narrow the report for a specific brand or collection of products.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:11.736
Click Show Filters and use the drop-down menu to select a brand, or enter up to 100 ASINs in the

00:04:11.736 --> 00:04:14.680
search bar separated by either a space or comma.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.440
Then click the Refine Results button to refresh the report.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:24.404
If you'd like to add or remove columns on the Search Catalog Performance Report, click Customize

00:04:24.404 --> 00:04:26.640
Columns on the right-hand side.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.400
Then check or uncheck boxes in the pop-up.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.860
Click the Save button to return to the updated report.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.260
To download a copy of the report, click the Generate Download button.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:44.251
Then in the pop-up, select either Simple View to download the report you see on screen or select

00:04:44.251 --> 00:04:47.720
Comprehensive View to download the report with all relevant columns.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.693
Click the Generate Download button to start your download, which you can monitor by accessing the

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.320
Download Manager.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.988
Finally, if you want more information about how a specific metric is calculated, click Metrics Glossary

00:05:00.988 --> 00:05:03.660
to see a set of comprehensive definitions.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:09.600
On the Metrics Glossary page, you can expand each section to see additional details.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:15.773
We encourage brands to use all the features and functionality of the Search Catalog Performance

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:19.640
Report to gain insights into their performance in the Amazon Store.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:25.620
Use drop-off points at the click stage to decide which product detail pages might need updating,

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:31.895
or use other metrics to develop advertising strategies that can help drive more traffic to your

00:05:31.895 --> 00:05:32.260
products.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.500
This concludes our overview of the Search Catalog Performance Report.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:43.364
If you'd like step-by-step instructions for other brand analytics reports, see our series of modules

00:05:43.364 --> 00:05:44.480
in Seller University.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.120
Thank you, and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
